  "status_text": "Five gates are too few for one way of making three lights blink when only two gates can flip bits. Lean checked that limit by turning five switches on in order and prescribing when each light shines (L-meta-50312). Now twelve four-switch cases put an extra bit flip to the test. Lean checked six-gate circuits using at most three NOTs for all twelve (L-lib-1325). The search asks whether two NOTs can match those patterns within six gates in ten cases and seven in two, starting at L-meta-53132.",
